index 8413d20ce..b9f79fb22 100644
--- a/changelog.d/pr-11392.md
+++ b/changelog.d/pr-11392.md
@@ -27,4 +27,7 @@ Since mhs ignores the `LANGUAGE` pragmas of the extensions it does not
 implement, packages are not rejected for the extensions they declare, and
 `reexported-modules` are accepted, as mhs sees all the modules of the
 packages it loads. The macros of `cabal_macros.h`, such as `MIN_VERSION_base`,
-are passed to mhs as `-D` options of its preprocessor.
+are passed to mhs as `-D` options of its preprocessor. If mhs has `ghc-compat`
+installed, as `mcabal install ghc-compat` does, every component is compiled
+with it, as MicroCabal does: it holds modules that are part of `base` in GHC,
+such as `GHC.Stack`.
